
==== 1  the scenario: how many collisions per bunch crossing =========================================
  Run 3 (2024, levelled): L = 2.00e+34 cm^-2 s^-1, sigma_inel = 78.42 mb (PYTHIA, CP5, the tune fixes it),
  n_b = 2350 colliding bunches, f_rev = 11245.5 Hz: 1.568e+09 collisions/s over 2.643e+07 crossings/s
  mu = L sigma / (n_b f_rev) = 59.3 (60.5 with the 80 mb of the bookkeeping); the mixing scenario rounds it to mu = 60 (CMSSW AVE_60_BX_25ns), window bx = -12 ... +3, 960 collisions expected per signal event
  the Run-3 production mixes Run3_Flat55To75_PoissonOOTPU: mu_true of the in-time crossing drawn flat in 55 ... 75 (mean 65), Poisson draws of the same mean in the other 15 crossings, about 1040 collisions per signal event; this record fixes mu_true = 60

==== 2  the draw of the MixingModule: Poisson(mu) collisions per bunch crossing ======================
  bx -12: 60, bx -11: 56, bx -10: 68, bx -9: 61, bx -8: 66, bx -7: 56, bx -6: 55, bx -5: 50, bx -4: 53, bx -3: 66, bx -2: 61, bx -1: 60, bx +0: 63, bx +1: 63, bx +2: 59, bx +3: 63; 960 collisions for an expectation of 960 (Poisson: 60 +- 7.7 per crossing)
  library: 2000 events, read in order from a random position (event 430), wrapping at the end; 960 distinct events used
  process types: CD 18, DD 86, ND 698, SD 158 (library shares: CD 1.9%, DD 10.9%, ND 71.2%, SD 15.9%)

==== 3  the beam spot: where and when each collision happens =========================================
  BetafuncEvtVtxGenerator with the 2024 payload (SimBeamSpot_Realistic25ns13p6TeVEarly2024CollisionVtxSmearingParameters_v1_mc):
  centre (0.0285, -0.0166, 0.416) cm, sigma_z = 3.6 cm, beta* = 30 cm, emittance 5.725e-08 cm: sigma_xy = 9.3 um at the focus, x sqrt(1 + ((z - z0)/beta*)^2) away from it (the hourglass)
  sigma_z, sigma_t of the model: 3.60 cm, 120 ps (sigma_t = sigma_z / c, z and t independent: what two head-on Gaussian bunches of 5.1 cm would give; the payload is a fit to the 2024 data, the crossing angle folded in)
  drawn: 960 vertices with r.m.s. x 8.9 um, y 9.6 um, z 3.56 cm (mean 0.22), t 124 ps; z from -12.4 to 13.9 cm
  the signal vertex: x = 287.1 um, y = -155.1 um, z = 0.16 cm, t = 94 ps; the out-of-time crossings are shifted by 25 ns x bx (the CMSSW signal event of the companion sits at z = 3.11 cm, t = +121 ps)

==== 4  the stacking: one final state out of the signal and the in-time crowd ========================
  the signal: 744 final particles without the neutrinos, 651 within |eta| < 5
  in-time (bx = 0): 63 collisions, 13456 final particles, 10045 within |eta| < 5 and not neutrinos; the mixed final state has 10696 particles
  particles per crossing: bx -12: 11013, bx -11: 9418, bx -10: 12855, bx -9: 11252, bx -8: 10912, bx -7: 9678, bx -6: 9360, bx -5: 9135, bx -4: 10755, bx -3: 11854, bx -2: 11887, bx -1: 9739, bx +0: 13456, bx +1: 11919, bx +2: 11036, bx +3: 10883; the out-of-time ones are recorded with their time offset and not clustered
  the in-time crowd in the tracker (|eta| < 2.5, pT > 0.5): 995 charged particles against 93 of the signal

==== 5  anti-kT on the mixed final state, with ghosts for the areas ==================================
  10696 particles + 6300 ghosts of area 0.0100 (|y| < 5): 16996 steps in 157 s; 175 jets above 3 GeV, 82 above 30
  the b jet: chapter-7 jet [0] 99.83 GeV, 31 particles -> mixed jet [1] 133.53 GeV, 115 particles (31 signal, 84 pileup from 33 collisions), dR = 0.012, area 0.529 (pi R^2 = 0.503); signal pT inside 100.07, pileup pT inside 34.57
    of the 31 particles of the photograph 31 are in the mixed jet, 0 fell out, 0 signal particles joined
  the bbar jet: chapter-7 jet [1] 94.09 GeV, 18 particles -> mixed jet [0] 136.77 GeV, 101 particles (19 signal, 82 pileup from 33 collisions), dR = 0.014, area 0.489 (pi R^2 = 0.503); signal pT inside 94.33, pileup pT inside 43.42

==== 6  the median energy density rho, two ways ======================================================
  grid median (fixedGridRhoFastjetAll): 18 x 11 cells of 0.556 x 0.571 = 0.317 in |y| < 5, phi from 0; rho = 75.47 GeV per unit area (cells from 30.0 to 361.5, mean 82.93)
  the same grid on the signal alone: rho = 3.42 (median; mean 11.08, 17 of 198 cells empty); on the crowd alone: rho = 69.93, so the signal raises the median by 5.53
  jet median (Cacciari-Salam): kT jets of R = 0.4 with ghosts, 195 jets, 171 within |y| < 4.4; rho = 78.50 GeV per unit area (pT/A from 41.7 to 236.9); 30 s
  per collision: 1.198 (grid) and 1.246 (jets) GeV per unit area

